        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edmond Harjo\n- Organizations: Seminole Nation of Oklahoma\n- Events: Normandy landings, Battle of Iwo Jima, Allied victory on the Western Front\n- Topics: Code talkers, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Edmond Harjo served with his brothers at the Normandy landings during World War II.\n- The Normandy landings were the largest seaborne invasion in history.\n- The Normandy landings began the liberation of German-occupied northwestern Europe from Nazi control.\n- The Normandy landings contributed to the Allied victory on the Western Front.\n- Edmond Harjo also served at the Battle of Iwo Jima during World War II.\n- Edmond Harjo was the last surviving code talker from the Seminole Nation of Oklahoma.",
